= V1 ontology maturation =

This audit applies the [[BITwiki:V1 to V2 maturation|V1 → V2 maturation sequence]] to ontology and classification:

'''preserve → understand → identify signal → mature primitive → enhance → integrate.'''

The purpose is not to decide whether V1's ontology was "right" or "wrong." V1 contains overlapping models developed through experimentation. The task is to identify durable functions inside those models, distinguish them from implementation reality, and express them through coherent V2 primitives.

== Evidence boundary ==

This audit distinguishes three evidence layers:

# '''Archived implementation''' — namespaces, pages, revisions, category memberships, template callers, and other objects preserved in <code>archive-v1/</code>.
# '''V1 design/source syntax''' — ontology, taxonomy, page-type, entity-type, relationship, property, interoperability specifications, and semantic examples, whether or not all proposed machinery was instantiated as a coherent production schema.
# '''Current V2 architecture''' — the source-reconciled semantic model in [[BITwiki:Ontology]], [[BITwiki:Entity types]], [[BITwiki:Relationships]], [[BITwiki:Semantic properties]], [[Property:Entity type]], [[Property:Domain]], Categories, Portals, and related standards.

A proposal or example in layer 2 is design/source evidence, not automatically proof of implementation in layer 1.

